-- Cause G — FFI opaque collapse to "Value".
--
-- Today every opaque FFI type from go-pkg gets collapsed to
-- (Canonical "") "Value" — so a Sky annotation `stripe.Customer`
-- and `aws.Account` unify even though they're distinct Go types.
-- The C17 6-commit umbrella (see docs/v0.17-c17-revised-design.md)
-- closes this; this fixture today GREEN-as-baseline and ready to
-- tighten to MUST_FAIL_BUILD on cross-package opaque shapes when
-- C17 lands.
--
-- Note: this fixture intentionally has NO FFI usage today — it
-- captures the baseline Sky-only behavior + reserves a slot in
-- the probe sweep for the cross-pkg opaque fixture once
-- examples/13-skyshop's stripe Customer / paymentMethod cross-shape
-- gets probed properly.
main =
    println "probe-G placeholder — see docs/v0.17-c17-revised-design.md"
